{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And also the priests.</b> Meaning, even though they possess the prerogative of drawing near to the sacred place to serve in the House of HaShem, as was transmitted in their hands — whether the firstborn or the seed of Aaron — <b>let them sanctify themselves</b>, meaning: their sanctity must not be regarded as extending as far as this boundary, and they need to reckon themselves in relation to this place as though they have no sanctity at all. And the measure of the word ״יִתְקַדָּשׁוּ״ is like the measure of the word ״וְדִשְּׁנוּ״ (Numbers 4:13). Or it may mean, according to the words of our Sages of blessed memory (Mekhilta), that He bounded the mountain: up to here Moses, up to here the boundary of Aaron, up to here the boundary of the priests. Accordingly, the verse says <b>those who approach HaShem</b>, meaning: their boundary on the mountain extends closer, which is not so for Israel; <b>let them sanctify themselves</b>, meaning: let them stand in their sanctity and not proceed to ascend further, lest, etc."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:30:21.139467457Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}